  ✅ [C1.2b-S1.6] objects.reorder(['contract','car']) changes the list order

── S2 · records ──
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.1] records.create without a title → title = the value of titleFieldKey ('plate'); the row sits in this system/object under the contact (parentType CONTACT) and the 6 values are stored in CustomRecordValue (recordType CUSTOM)
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.2] records.get round-trips every value (TEXT · NUMBER · DATE · SELECT · BOOLEAN · LOOKUP) keyed by field key, plus the title
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.3] title follows titleFieldKey on update (plate changed → title changed; another field changed → title kept) and an explicit title on create wins over titleFieldKey
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.4] records.list({parentId}) returns the parent's records (3 created under c1) and `q` searches the title
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.5] records.archive sets archivedAt (the row is kept) and the default list hides it
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.6] a parent of the WRONG TYPE (a company / a member for a CONTACT object), an unknown parent id, and a missing parent for a CONTACT object are all VALIDATION (Thai message) and create nothing
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.7] records.move re-parents the record (parentId = the new contact AND partyId re-inherited from it); moving to a parent of the wrong type is VALIDATION and changes nothing
  ✅ [C1.2b-S2.8] timelineFor(recordId) answers for a record of this system (array or {items}) — it is the data source of the record page

